.TH GENESYS-WORKER 1 "2026-08-20" "GenESyS" "GenESyS Manual"
.SH NAME
genesys-worker \- GenESyS HTTP worker runtime
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B genesys-worker
.RI [ --port
.IR port ]
.RI [ --max-requests
.IR count ]
.RI [ application-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B genesys-worker
is the stable public entry point for the GenESyS HTTP worker. It is a small
wrapper that execs
.BR /usr/libexec/genesys/genesys-dispatch (8)
with
.BR "--app genesys-worker" .
The dispatcher selects either the validated per-user runtime referenced by
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
or the Debian-provided system fallback installed at
.I /usr/libexec/genesys/system/bin/genesys-worker
and then replaces itself with the selected worker executable. All arguments
given to
.B genesys-worker
are forwarded unchanged to the selected executable.
.PP
The worker is designed for a controlled academic intranet and is not intended
for direct public-Internet exposure. It never performs a network update
check; update behavior is exclusive to
.BR genesys-gui (1).
.SH OPTIONS
The system fallback worker executable currently accepts at least:
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Listen on the given TCP port on the loopback/bound interface instead of the
default port.
.TP
.BI --max-requests " count"
Serve at most the given number of requests before exiting.
.SH ENDPOINTS
.TP
.B /health
Returns a JSON liveness document while the worker is running.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/genesys/update.conf
System-wide administrative runtime-selection policy (conffile).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/genesys/current
Symbolic link selecting the active per-user runtime, if any.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the selected worker executable, or 127 if no valid runtime
could be selected.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR genesys-gui (1),
.BR genesys-web (1)
